{title: 626 - In a Little While We're Going Home}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Let us sing a song that will cheer us by the way,
[Eb]In a little while we’re going [Bb]home;
[Bb]For the [Bb7]night will end in the [Eb]everlasting day,
[Eb]In a little [Fm/Ab]while we’re going [Eb/Bb]home.

Refrain:
[Bb]In a [Eb]little while, In [Bb7]a little while,
[Bb7]We shall cross [Eb]the billow's foam;
[Eb]We shall meet at last, When the [Bb7/D]stormy [Cm]winds are [Bb]past,
[Eb]In a little while [Ab]we're going home.

Verse 2:
[Eb]We will do the work that our hands may find to do,
[Eb]In a little while we're going [Bb]home.
[Bb]And the [Bb7]grace of God will our [Eb]daily strength renew,
[Eb]In a little [Fm/Ab]while we're going [Eb/Bb]home.

Verse 3:
[Eb]We will smooth the path for some weary, wayworn feet,
[Eb]In a little while we're going [Bb]home.
[Bb]And may [Bb7]loving hearts spread around [Eb]an influence sweet!
[Eb]In a little [Fm/Ab]while we're going [Eb/Bb]home.

Verse 4:
[Eb]There's a rest beyond, there's relief from every care,
[Eb]In a little while we're going [Bb]home;
[Bb]And no [Bb7]tears shall fall in that [Eb]city bright and fair,
[Eb]In a little [Fm/Ab]while we're going [Eb/Bb]home.
